urity measures, so the harnessed commercial models do not have to do what they cannot\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/da1e3f/vision/operational-coreSoulCluster.md:7:> For now, we're just going to have this simple system of psyche, mind, codex, and cloud, and let's get that third open source portion so we can run the core. I want a core soul cluster that's going to give the personality and drive the basic security measures of setting all this up so that the models here who have a hard time doing this stuff don't have to do it. The models that can do it can do it on an open source harness that we control better.\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/b81560/vision/archive-operational-pocSandboxVmFirst.md:1:# Operational: a proof of concept should be tested in a sandbox VM first — exception when credentials require the host browser\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/b81560/vision/archive-operational-pocSandboxVmFirst.md:3:## A proof of concept should be tested in a sandbox in a virtual machine. But because we need to log in in the browser with my credentials, and you can't really run this in a virtual machine\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/b81560/vision/archive-operational-pocSandboxVmFirst.md:8:is when the living's own browser credentials are needed for login, which\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/b81560/vision/archive-operational-pocSandboxVmFirst.md:12:> Well, I would say yes, this is good, but first, a proof of concept should be tested in a sandbox in a virtual machine. But because we need to log in in the browser with my credentials, and you can't really run this in a virtual machine\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/f38926/vision/operational-openCodeRemoteAccess.md:13:## A proof of concept should be tested in a sandbox in a virtual machine; this one needs a browser login with my credentials, which can't run in a virtual machine\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/f38926/vision/operational-openCodeRemoteAccess.md:17:> Well, I would say yes, this is good, but first, a proof of concept should be tested in a sandbox in a virtual machine. But because we need to log in in the browser with my credentials, and you can't really run this in a virtual machine\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/fd0f97/vision/persona.md:1:# Persona\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/fd0f97/vision/persona.md:3:## Every major idea of the vision finds its place in the Persona meta-harness and is made to happen, over a few waves of rebootstrapping if needed, the flow going on independently for days\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/fd0f97/vision/persona.md:7:> Find the right place for all the major ideas of the vision we've put together now for this persona meta harness, and let's make it happen. If it takes a few waves of rebootstrapping, go ahead. Maybe you go on independently for a few days.\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/f38926/vision/refresh.md:3:## Every refreshed or new session starts in Herdr, with an exact live pane binding, before its HM messaging is trusted\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/f38926/vision/refresh.md:7:> every refreshed/new session must START IN HERDR, with exact live pane binding before HM messaging is trusted\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/fd0f97/vision/launch.md:15:## A main flow should always be made remotely controllable; the main flow type serves all the clusters of durable flows in the different layers of Persona\n/home/li/wt/primary/mind-sol-successor-56ae53-target/flows/fd0f97/vision/launch.md:19:> So we should always make it remotely controllable, right? Do we know how to do that? How to make sure that this main flow, this main flow type of thing, which is for all the clusters of durable