all, which is why d8df70 and\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:200:  e51411 stayed listed Pending after messenger-clj had retired them\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:203:  Presented Send *or* List finding its bound pane present in Herdr. Only a\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:205:  `MetaBindExisting` or started before Flow Nexus stayed Pending for as long\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:206:  as it lived: of fifteen listed flows only four read Active while every Mind\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:209:- A plain `Start` answers `Started` for a launch that succeeds. It used to\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:210:  answer `StartAmbiguous` the instant the first prompt was submitted, leaving\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:213:  already watching the seat's transcript — so Start waits for the launch to\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:217:  the bound (three minutes) and is answered `StartAmbiguous`, which the\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:226:  outright. When the stored flow is that binding (not Stopped; the same native\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:227:  thread and harness; a route on the same Herdr session, pane and terminal,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:238:  its Herdr pane alone. `MetaBindExisting` stores its Codex endpoint as\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:241:  Herdr route and the endpoint as separate facts, Send types into the pane when\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:282:  connection (`SO_PEERCRED`), never a field of the request; its Herdr pane is\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:283:  read from `HERDR_SESSION` and `HERDR_PANE_ID` in its `/proc` environment,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:290:  Start (from the launch profile). A flow registered through the meta\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:298:  launched by Start (5f38bc, 88475f) keep no role and resolve\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:309:  replaced by `NotDelivered`: Herdr refused before any input reached the pane\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:316:- `Sent.Presented` now means Herdr's `agent prompt --wait` saw the settled\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:318:  `{ FlowId HerdrPaneId PresentationObservedUnixMilliseconds }`; the marker\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:331:real Claude Start (successor 88475f, launched through 0.10.5):\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:333:- A receipt that arrives after `StartAmbiguous` now promotes the launch with\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:334:  no subscriber and no second Start. The Nexus runs its own watch over every\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:335:  ambiguous launch (on startup too, so a launch left ambiguous by an older\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:338:- The Claude receipt observer stops checking once the first turn and every\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:344:- A Herdr route is keyed on the session, pane id and terminal id. The agent\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:345:  name is re-read from the snapshot (ResolveRecipient, Send and Stop report\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:358:A patch release with no wire, storage or argv-shape change. The Herdr route\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:362:  before) is routable when its Herdr `agent_status` is `idle`, `done` or\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:364:  `idle` or `done`. Herdr 0.8.2 reports a harness at rest after a turn as\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:366:- `interactive_ready` gates the route only when Herdr reports it: an absent\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:367:  (or null) flag permits, `true` permits, any other value refuses. Herdr 0.8.2\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:382:  outcome is stored, or when the Flow the launch bound is stopped (`Stop`, or\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:383:  the reap of a `Replace`). A Started Flow keeps its copy while it runs.\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:394:per launch. At Start the Nexus writes each Claude launch its own copy of the\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:400:bundle is never edited. A copy that cannot be written refuses Start as\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:406:Herdr from an absent pane. A failed or roster-less snapshot of the\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:425:  Start answers as `CompositionRefused`.\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:434:predecessor whose pane is already gone from Herdr as already reaped: the\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:435:predecessor is recorded `Stopped`, `Replaced` is recorded, and the successor\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:453:- Start sets the canonical native title `<Aspect>V2.{ <Model> <FlowId> }`\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:454:  and the Herdr pane label after the claim and reads both back before any\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:456:  model-display map; an unmapped model refuses the Start (`BindingRefused`).\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:459:- Claude starts with `--settings '{\"permissions\":{\"defaultMode\":\"bypassPermissions\"}}'`,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:468:  is recorded `Stopped` and its pane closed before the successor is routable.\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:472:- `ResolveRecipient` now refuses a `Stopped` flow with `FlowUnavailable`.\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:476:  and `FLOW_CODEX_*` deployment overrides still apply at start.\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:498:A fresh Flow now receives one prompt. The native harness starts with no\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:499:positional startup block; the composed first prompt carries the native skill\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:UPGRADES.md:522:Flow stores and starts Flow 0.4.0 with a fresh store. A privileged caller then\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:41:                let Some(herdr_session_name) = arguments.next() else { return Err(Self::registration_usage()) };\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:42:                let Some(herdr_agent_name) = arguments.next() else { return Err(Self::registration_usage()) };\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:43:                let Some(herdr_pane_id) = arguments.next() else { return Err(Self::registration_usage()) };\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:44:                let Some(herdr_terminal_id) = arguments.next() else { return Err(Self::registration_usage()) };\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:76:                    herdr_route_selection: signal_flow::HerdrRouteSelection::Available(\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:77:                        signal_flow::HerdrRoute {\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:78:                            herdr_session_name,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:79:                            herdr_agent_name,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:80:                            herdr_pane_id,\nbc464e5e1b94fcc179af73111f43b69db1f69fc5:crates/flow-meta/src/main.rs:81:                            her